### Conflict Analysis

| # | Conflict | Severity | Resolution |
|---|----------|----------|------------|
| 1 | **Two `BaseAgent` designs** — Yours uses `Event/AgentAction/AuditEntry` with permissions & approval queue. Friends' uses simpler `(name, event_bus)` with `on_start/on_stop`. | 🟡 Medium | Keep your richer `BaseAgent`. Adapt friends' agents to extend it. |
| 2 | **Two `Event` schema designs** — Yours has `EventType` enum. Friends' uses plain `str` type. | 🟡 Medium | Keep yours, add new event types for MIS/Orchestrateur/Qualité. |
| 3 | **Three `EventBus` implementations** — Yours: Redis Streams. Friend 1: InMemory only. Friend 2: InMemory + Kafka + Redis pub/sub. | 🟢 Low | Merge Friend 2's `KafkaEventBus` + configurable factory into your `shared/event_bus.py`. Keep your Redis Streams as default. |
| 4 | **Port collision** — All three FastAPI apps default to port 8000. | 🟢 Low | Only your `api/main.py` runs. Friends' `main.py` files won't be used. |
| 5 | **Docker services overlap** — All three have Postgres on 5432; Friend 2 adds Kafka on 9092. | 🟢 Low | Consolidate into your root `docker-compose.yml`. Add Kafka if needed. |
| 6 | **Frontend replacement** — Your current `frontend/` is a minimal scaffold. The new Figma frontend is production-ready with auth, API hooks, and full UI. | 🟢 Low | Delete old `frontend/`, replace with new one. |
| 7 | **LLM Client** — Yours is async. Friend 2's is synchronous with structured prompting for Qualité eval + Orchestrateur routing. | 🟡 Medium | Merge Friend 2's domain-specific LLM functions into your async `llm_client.py`. |
| 8 | **Veille RAG Pipeline** — Friend 1 has a standalone `veille-agent/` with PubMed fetcher, embedder, and RAG. | 🟢 Low | Merge into `agents/veille/services/`. |

